MARS ETHEREUM NODE
==================

This directory keeps the local Ethereum node setup inside the MARS repo.
The scripts are tracked. The node database is not.

Default data directory:

    node/data/mainnet

Initialize:

    node/bin/init-mainnet.sh

Then run these in two terminals:

    node/bin/start-geth-mainnet.sh
    node/bin/start-lighthouse-mainnet.sh

MARS reads Geth over the local JSON-RPC endpoint:

    export ETH_RPC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8545

Sanity check:

    curl -s "$ETH_RPC_URL" \
      -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
      -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"eth_blockNumber","params":[],"id":1}'

If the repo disk is too small, keep the command surface here but point the data
directory at a large external SSD:

    node/bin/init-mainnet.sh /Volumes/ETHNODE/mars-eth
    node/bin/start-geth-mainnet.sh /Volumes/ETHNODE/mars-eth
    node/bin/start-lighthouse-mainnet.sh /Volumes/ETHNODE/mars-eth

Ethereum mainnet requires both clients:

    geth        execution client and JSON-RPC endpoint for MARS
    lighthouse consensus client that drives post-merge sync

The initializer refuses disks with less than 700 GiB free by default. Override
only when you know the target disk can support the sync:

    MARS_ETH_MIN_FREE_GIB=500 node/bin/init-mainnet.sh
